00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:52.720
let's take a look at the ordinary sulphate&nbsp;
4% cleanser for body and hair which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.800
a pretty stripped back shampoo formula

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:59.280
sodium laureth sulfate is the anionic&nbsp;
surfactant it's at four percent which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:04.640
you can hopefully tell from the name this is&nbsp;
pretty low for shampoo but this also doubles up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:09.120
as a body wash which normally has&nbsp;
lower amounts so this keeps it gentle

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:11.760
specifically they're using sles-2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.600
which means there's two ethoxy units&nbsp;
